@page
@model ForestChurches.Pages.faqModel
@{
}
<head>
    <link href="~/css2/Page-header.css" integrity="sha256-Rtz0HIcRj9MQNF8G3xzx3+XNkldfHcYBgrvQhm9r6qY=" rel="stylesheet" />
    <style nonce="@HttpContextAccessor.HttpContext?.Items["CSP-Style-Nonce"]">
        .headers {
            color: white;
        }
        main {
            background-color: #00AD6A;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<div class="container-fluid page-hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
        <h1>Frequenty Asked Questions</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="container marketing">
    <!--Section: FAQ-->
    <section>
        <h3 class="text-center mb-4 pb-2 headers fw-bold">FAQ</h3>
        <p class="text-center mb-5">
            Find the answers for the most frequently asked questions below
        </p>

        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    How do i register my church?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    You can register your church by getting in contact with us using our 
                    <a asp-page="/Contact">Contact Us</a> page. We will then send a unique invitation 
                    link to your email where you will be able to create an account. 
                    Upon registration, a church is automatically generated and assigned to your user. 
                    You can then edit this to present your church information by going to your <a asp-page="../Identity/Pages/Manage/ChurchProfile">Church Profile</a>.
                </p>
            </div>
            <!-- <a asp-page="./Add/Index" class="btn btn-success add-event-btn">Add Event</a> -->
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    There are other services that do the same thing, why should i use this one?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    Yes, there are many other services that can profile a church and advertise it. 
                    However, in many cases this comes at a cost, whith the added task of trying to 
                    find out what church is nearest. This app costs nothing (and never will). 
                    The aim of this app is to provide a localized version to help people in the 
                    Forest Of Dean find out about a nearby church or even ann event, hosted by a church.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    Why can't I directly download my personal information?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    Your personal information is available at any point in time. 
                    While it's true, you cannot currenty access it directly, 
                    one of our support team members would be more than happy to 
                    provide you with your personal data should you ask for it. 
                    Simply send us a message using our <a asp-page="/Contact">Contact Us</a> page.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    Where are you storing my data?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    To enure the safety and security of your data. 
                    All information is stored in an external database, 
                    which is only accessible to the application itself.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    My event dissapeared from my church?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    To minimlize the data stored and help keep costs down, 
                    events will be automatically deleted up to 24 hours after an event has completed. 
                    Repeated events remain on the system, however you will recieve the occasional email, 
                    confirming whether you still want this event.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    How do I update my Church information?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    You can update your church information in your <a asp-page="../Identity/Pages/Manage/ChurchProfile">Church Profile</a>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    Why can't i change the email address on my account?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    For security reasons, we have removed the ability for users to change the email address of their accounts. 
                    If you wish to update your email, please get in touch with us and we would be happy to help.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    Why isn't the link in my email working anymore?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    The majority of links that you will recieve from us
                    by email are encrypted and will only last 24 hours at a time.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4 mb-4">
                <h4 class="mb-3 headers">
                    Why do some pages notifiy me of changes and others do not?
                </h4>
                <p>
                    The website is still in it's early stage of release, therefore a few bugs are to be expected. 
                    The plan is that every page presents the StatusMessage upon completion of an action.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
